WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.153
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:14.857
Unit ten: Technology Basics. Today you will give advice about using devices.

4
00:00:15.157 --> 00:00:17.739
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.014
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:23.874
Device.

7
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:28.044
Device means a machine or tool like a phone or tablet.

8
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.708
Turn off your device in class.

9
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:33.597
Your turn. Say: Device.

10
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:37.446
Device.

11
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:39.289
Application.

12
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:44.071
Application means a program on a phone or computer; an app.

13
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:47.170
This application helps me learn words.

14
00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:50.784
Your turn. Say: Application.

15
00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:54.890
Application.

16
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:56.512
Update.

17
00:00:57.517 --> 00:01:00.190
Update means a new version that fixes problems.

18
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.829
Install the update tonight.

19
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:06.115
Your turn. Say: Update.

20
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:09.886
Update.

21
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:11.767
Notification.

22
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:16.095
Notification means a message that tells you something new.

23
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:18.938
Turn off notifications when you study.

24
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.237
Your turn. Say: Notification.

25
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.380
Notification.

26
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:27.909
Battery.

27
00:01:28.917 --> 00:01:31.311
Battery means the part that stores power.

28
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.114
My battery is almost empty.

29
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:37.032
Your turn. Say: Battery.

30
00:01:39.867 --> 00:01:40.659
Battery.

31
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.453
Wireless.

32
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.763
Wireless means working without cables.

33
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.257
I use wireless headphones.

34
00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:51.537
Your turn. Say: Wireless.

35
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.529
Wireless.

36
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:57.261
Storage.

37
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.318
Storage means space to keep files and photos.

38
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:03.928
My phone has no storage left.

39
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:06.972
Your turn. Say: Storage.

40
00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:10.927
Storage.

41
00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.441
Backup.

42
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.960
Backup means an extra copy of your files.

43
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.364
Make a backup of your photos.

44
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.498
Your turn. Say: Backup.

45
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.451
Backup.

46
00:02:26.217 --> 00:02:27.148
Troubleshoot.

47
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.823
Troubleshoot means to find and fix problems.

48
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.196
Let's troubleshoot the printer.

49
00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:36.262
Your turn. Say: Troubleshoot.

50
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.124
Troubleshoot.

51
00:02:40.883 --> 00:02:41.931
Interface.

52
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:46.356
Interface means the screen design you use to control a program.

53
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.135
The new interface is easy to use.

54
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.333
Your turn. Say: Interface.

55
00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.319
Interface.

56
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.131
Shortcut.

57
00:02:59.117 --> 00:03:01.395
Shortcut means a quick way to do something.

58
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:04.227
Ctrl C is a shortcut for copy.

59
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.411
Your turn. Say: Shortcut.

60
00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:11.314
Shortcut.

61
00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.248
Malfunction.

62
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.155
Malfunction means to stop working correctly.

63
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.458
My laptop malfunctioned during the test.

64
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.842
Your turn. Say: Malfunction.

65
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.189
Malfunction.

66
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.860
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:33.717 --> 00:03:35.530
Visal, your phone looks slow.

68
00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:40.625
Yes, the storage is full, and the battery dies fast.

69
00:03:41.717 --> 00:03:44.181
You should delete old videos and make a backup.

70
00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:48.458
Good idea. Should I install the update too?

71
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.260
Yes! You shouldn't ignore updates.

72
00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:57.047
OK. I should turn off some notifications too.

73
00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.700
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.722
Grammar focus: should and shouldn't for advice.

75
00:04:04.022 --> 00:04:05.302
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:06.017 --> 00:04:07.714
You should back up your files.

77
00:04:08.617 --> 00:04:10.280
You shouldn't ignore updates.

78
00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.090
You should charge your battery at night.

79
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:17.580
'Back up' (two words) is the verb. 'Backup' (one word) is the noun.

80
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:21.689
Be careful! Don't say: You should to update your phone.

81
00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:25.807
Say: You should update your phone.

82
00:04:26.107 --> 00:04:27.654
Don't use 'to' after 'should'.

83
00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:31.537
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:34.112
Taking Care of My Phone.

85
00:04:34.412 --> 00:04:37.677
My phone's battery drains fast because of notifications.

86
00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.955
Last month, it malfunctioned, and I lost some photos.

87
00:04:42.967 --> 00:04:45.512
Now I always make a backup of my files.

88
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.833
I should install updates, and I shouldn't fill my storage with old videos.

89
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:54.553
When there is a problem, I try to troubleshoot it myself.

90
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:59.483
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:00.317 --> 00:05:02.003
You blank ignore updates.

92
00:05:02.303 --> 00:05:05.643
A, shouldn't. B, should. C, don't should.

93
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.944
The answer is A: shouldn't.

94
00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:14.570
An extra copy of your files is a blank.

95
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.431
A, backup. B, shortcut. C, battery.

96
00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:23.722
The answer is A: backup.

97
00:05:24.883 --> 00:05:27.289
To find and fix problems is to blank.

98
00:05:27.589 --> 00:05:31.243
A, troubleshoot. B, update. C, malfunction.

99
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.718
The answer is A: troubleshoot.

100
00:05:37.933 --> 00:05:41.201
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.456
What technology device do you use the most?

102
00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.727
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:55.027 --> 00:06:02.512
I use my phone the most. I use it for learning apps and messages. I should turn off notifications when I study.

104
00:06:02.812 --> 00:06:04.660
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:10.141
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and should and shouldn't for advice.

106
00:06:10.441 --> 00:06:15.067
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

107
00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.869
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:22.040
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

